What actually needs to move
Code: from GitHub (git@github.com:farjlcn1/teren.git or wherever it ends up)
Secrets (gitignored, not in the repo): .env (just POSTGRES_PASSWORD) and .env.production (SESSION_SECRET, UPLOADS_DIR, SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASSWORD/FROM, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL)
Database: the postgres_data Docker volume (all clients, users, work orders)
Uploaded files: /home/matija/teren-data/uploads (photos, signatures), bind-mounted into the container
A dependency you might miss: SMTP currently goes through host.docker.internal → this laptop's own local Postfix relay. The new machine won't have that unless you set it up too.
Public exposure: the app only binds to 127.0.0.1:3000 — it's never directly reachable, it relies entirely on the Cloudflare Tunnel.
Decisions to make before starting
Migrate existing data, or start fresh? (I'll assume migrate, since you said "stop running it here and start it there")
New domain — is it on Cloudflare already, or a different registrar/DNS provider?
Mail: replicate the Postfix relay on the new machine, or point SMTP_HOST at something else reachable from there?
Phase 1 — On this machine: package up the data
docker compose --project-directory /home/matija/farjolcn/teren exec -T postgres pg_dump -U teren teren > teren-db.sql
tar czf teren-uploads.tar.gz -C /home/matija/teren-data uploads
cp /home/matija/farjolcn/teren/.env /home/matija/farjolcn/teren/.env.production teren-env-backup/

Move teren-db.sql, teren-uploads.tar.gz, and the two env files to the new machine (scp/USB — treat the env files as secrets, not something to paste into chat).

Phase 2 — New machine: prerequisites
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose-plugin git

(needs an interactive terminal for sudo — run it yourself)

Phase 3 — Clone and restore
git clone git@github.com:farjlcn1/teren.git
cp .env .env.production teren/
mkdir -p ~/teren-data/uploads && tar xzf teren-uploads.tar.gz -C ~/teren-data
Phase 4 — Update docker-compose.yml for this machine's paths

Change the uploads bind mount if the path differs from /home/matija/teren-data/uploads (e.g. different username). Everything else in docker-compose.yml is portable as-is.

Phase 5 — Update .env.production for the new domain
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="https://your-new-domain.com"

And either point SMTP_HOST at a relay reachable from the new machine, or set up Postfix there too.

Phase 6 — Bring up empty containers, then restore the DB
docker compose up -d postgres
cat teren-db.sql | docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U teren -d teren
docker compose up -d --build app

The entrypoint runs prisma migrate deploy automatically on start, so schema stays in sync.

Phase 7 — Cloudflare Tunnel for the new domain
cloudflared tunnel login
cloudflared tunnel create teren-new
cloudflared tunnel route dns teren-new your-new-domain.com

Then a config.yml mapping that hostname → http://localhost:3000, and a systemd unit to run it persistently (same pattern as this machine's farjolcn-laptop tunnel).

Phase 8 — Verify before cutting over

Load https://your-new-domain.com directly, log in, confirm data/photos are there, send a test action that triggers email, before touching anything on this machine.
